# Defaults for nektos/act (installed here as `gh act`).
#
# --bind is what makes the e2e suite work: the container sees the workspace at
# the same absolute path as the host, so whatever the fake cloud writes inside
# is readable by pytest outside, with no artifact plumbing.
#
# --container-daemon-socket - stops act bind-mounting the Docker socket, which
# fails outright on colima ("operation not supported"). Nothing here needs a
# real daemon: the e2e suite shims `docker`.
--container-architecture linux/amd64
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
--bind
--container-daemon-socket -
--pull=false
--action-offline-mode
